Package: SafeShiny
Type: Package
Title: Safe Observers for Shiny with Execution-Time Tracking
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(person("Venelin", "Mitov", email = "vmitov@gmail.com",
                    role = c("aut", "cre", "cph")))
Maintainer: Venelin Mitov <vmitov@gmail.com>
Description: An uncaught error inside a plain shiny::observe()/observeEvent() terminates the
  whole Shiny session, unlike an error inside a reactive() consumed only by a render output,
  which Shiny already converts into a localized, session-surviving error display. SafeShiny
  provides SafeObserve() and SafeObserveEvent(), drop-in replacements for shiny::observe() and
  shiny::observeEvent() that catch errors instead of letting them propagate, while correctly
  re-raising shiny::req()/shiny::validate()'s intentional silent-stop conditions unchanged.
  Both also support optional execution-time tracking, to separate time spent in application
  business logic from time spent in Shiny's own reactive-graph maintenance.
